# Infrastructure Templates

Purpose:
  Predefined infrastructure templates for provisioning workflows.

Skill: Infrastructure Templates

ID:
  PROMPT-INFRASTRUCTURE-TEMPLATES

Domain:
  prompts/provisioning

Use:
  predefined infrastructure templates for provisioning

Apply:
  provisioning
  infrastructure-setup
  deployment

Requires:
  terraform
  docker
  kubernetes

Avoid:
  hardcoded-values
  public-networking
  missing-security
  over-provisioning

Level:
  L2

Status:
  STABLE

Maturity:
  MATURE

Risk:
  MEDIUM

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  infrastructure templates
  terraform
  docker compose
  kubernetes manifests
  provisioning

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/prompts/infrastructure-templates.md

Evidence:
  - Terraform Registry
  - Docker Documentation
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [I1] All templates MUST use variables for configuration.
  [I2] All templates MUST include security best practices.
  [I3] All templates MUST be tested before use.
  [I4] All templates MUST include monitoring setup.
  [I5] All templates MUST be version controlled.

Templates:
  postgresql:
    path: terraform/postgresql
    components:
      - RDS instance
      - Parameter group
      - Security group
      - Backup policy
  redis:
    path: terraform/redis
    components:
      - ElastiCache cluster
      - Security group
      - Parameter group
  kafka:
    path: terraform/kafka
    components:
      - MSK cluster
      - Security group
      - Monitoring
  kubernetes:
    path: terraform/kubernetes
    components:
      - EKS/GKE/AKS cluster
      - Node groups
      - IAM roles
      - Networking

Pros:
  - Consistent infrastructure
  - Faster provisioning
  - Reduced errors

Cons:
  - Template maintenance
  - Less flexibility
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Manual provisioning
  - Console-based setup

State: +
